# OS metadata
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor scratch
*.swp
*~

# Office and cloud-sync lock files, and partial downloads.
# These belong to no one, and a blanket "stage everything" sweeps them into commits.
~$*
.~lock.*
*.tmp
*.crdownload
*.partial

# The scratch plane (STANDARD.md → Rule 6 → "Three planes"): a declared, wipeable workspace for
# temporarily materialized records (batch processing), with a stated lifetime. Git never holds
# it, so erasure is honored by construction. Wipe it when the batch completes.
_scratch/

# Python virtual environments (added in v1.51, drafted and unpublished). The shared renderer
# (tools/km-publish.sh) builds its environment outside the tree, so a hub normally generates nothing
# here. This rule covers the two cases where one lands in the hub anyway: an operator who points
# KM_PUBLISH_VENV back inside the tree, and a hub that ran the pre-v1.51 publisher, which built
# tools/.venv with no ignore rule anywhere and made the hub fail its own [ INTEGRITY ] check at every
# session start afterwards. Audit finding F-10.
.venv/
